  "notes": "LA’s lo-fi sample-chopper. The parameter is **deliberate imprecision**: snare and clap placed early or late by a 32nd, an extra unquantised kick, hats crushed or absent, and bit-reduction and tape saturation treated as part of the drum *timbre* rather than as a mix decision. Loops are 1–2 bars and **often harmonically incomplete on purpose**, so the harmony is entirely sample-inherited — 7ths, 9ths and unresolved changes. ⚠ `medium`: the sampling aesthetic and his role are documented; specific drum and tempo values are inferred and marked `[LOW-CONF]`. ⚠ A progression family authored `Imaj7`, which `Numeral::parse` cannot read — it knows i, VI, bII and vii° and takes the seventh from `chords.extensions`, not from the numeral. An unreadable numeral makes the generator skip the slot, so that whole family produced NO CHORDS AT ALL, and chords.rs caught it only when a seed happened to pick it. Now `I`; the major-7th colour is carried by the extensions block, where it was always meant to be.",
